sequenceDiagram
  %% Current capacity flow: task copies take no CI place. proof:run shares CI places with runner jobs and uses copies of the proof default, including available warm copies. The capacity and cleanup contract belongs to docs/cli/proof/run.mdx.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: development pipeline · copy capacity
  %% kind: pipeline.capacity
  autonumber
  %% lane T icon=server pill=task tone=gray
  %% lane PR icon=server pill=PR tone=purple
  %% lane Q icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane CP icon=server pill=capacity tone=amber
  %% lane PC icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  participant T as Task copy<br/>own nested fleet
  participant PR as Pull request<br/>proven feature
  participant Q as Proof queue<br/>Operation order
  participant CP as CI Nodes<br/>jobs and copies
  participant PC as Proof copies<br/>assigned batches
  Note over T: Build and prove first<br/>no CI place held
  T->>PR: Publish the feature<br/>after local proof passes
  opt CI proof enabled and selected
    PR->>Q: Confirm the PR head<br/>proof:run COMMIT
    %%> When:
    %%> - ORBIT_PROOF_ENABLED is deliberately off until commands have been checked systematically
    Q->>CP: Read free CI places<br/>runner state · memory · seed
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - takes no busy runner's place; available warm copies already hold their place and memory
    alt capacity is available
      CP-->>Q: Available copies<br/>warm or new from seed
      Q->>PC: Assign the batches<br/>balance by measured time
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - prepares the tested commit; each copy has its own nested fleet
      PC->>PC: Reset and run cases<br/>per assigned batch
      PC-->>Q: Verdict per case<br/>complete reports
      Q->>CP: Destroy the copies<br/>release holds on success
      %%> Result:
      %%> - every run end requests cleanup, including failures and cancellation; failed destruction keeps its hold until recovery succeeds
      Q-->>PR: One merged result<br/>all selected cases required
    else no free place
      Note over Q: Wait within the allowance<br/>120 minutes from creation
      %%> Result:
      %%> - capacity timeout fails; waiting or running no selected case never counts as proof
    end
  end
